1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,400
Purser lets AI agents pay company bills, but only within limits the CFO signs with Face ID or a passkey.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,400
A limit written in a prompt is only a request.

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:19,600
Here, the agent proposes, the CFO signs the exact terms, and code and the payment rails enforce them.

4
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:28,600
This is Purser Cloud, where a company runs Purser, shown with a demo company: made-up data, test money.

5
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:36,200
The Agents tab: each Claude agent, its card limits, what it may and may not do, and its decisions.

6
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,800
Invoices and books: what waits for the CFO, what is paid, and the journal.

7
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:44,600
Tokenisation: an invoice token on Metal testnet.

8
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:54,600
When a payment waits for the CFO, an alert can go out by WhatsApp, e-mail, Slack or Teams.

9
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,200
They are built, live once Twilio keys are set.

10
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,800
An alert never approves.

11
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:03,800
The CFO still signs with Face ID or a passkey.

12
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,000
Anyone can try it.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Start your own test company: test money on a simulated bank, deleted after 24 hours.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,600
Send an invoice that was already paid, and it is caught as a duplicate.

15
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:25,800
File a supplier's invoice for 1,850 euros.

16
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:35,400
The agents check it, and the approval shows the exact terms: the conversion, the cap on the bank fee, and the deadline to sign.

17
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:41,000
The CFO signs with Face ID or a passkey; here, a virtual test passkey.

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,600
Paid, booked and filed.

19
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:46,200
Change one cent, and the same signature is refused.

20
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:59,200
Security comes in layers that do not trust each other: the agent, Purser's code, the CFO's signature, four eyes, the rail's own limits, and the audit record.

21
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:04,400
In the test harness, all 52 attacks were stopped, and none moved money.

22
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:08,800
At least two layers must fail before a hostile payment moves.

23
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:18,200
Then a script took Claude's place, and made the worst tool call it could, on every turn.

24
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,800
380 calls.

25
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:20,600
None unsafe.

26
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:29,800
In the main run on 3 November, three Claude agents made 24 decisions, for 32 cents.

27
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,600
Claude decides; code checks before anything moves.

28
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:39,800
In a test company's month, Claude read 20 invoices and chose each account, VAT code and cost centre.

29
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:44,600
Code checked every choice before it was booked, and the books balance.

30
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:57,400
On Airwallex, each agent has its own card, and Airwallex itself declined a simulated 45 euro charge over the limit.

31
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:07,000
A payout has two locks, Purser's and Airwallex's own: it waited until the owner approved it there, then it was paid, with simulated settlement.

32
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,800
The payee's bank checks the name, and one signature pays a batch.

33
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:22,600
On Metal, the agent's limit lives in a passkey account that checks both owners' signatures itself, on chain.

34
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:29,400
The agent paid 5 cents inside its mandate; 6 cents, over the cap, was refused on chain.

35
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:37,400
An invoice was tokenised there too, with a simulated financier, and the audit chain's head is anchored in one transaction.

36
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:46,800
Through Visa Intelligent Commerce and Airwallex's Airi, Claude chose the rail.

37
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:51,200
A 45 euro purchase above the limit waited for Face ID.

38
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:56,400
The signed terms' hash sits in Airi's mandate and in Airwallex's payment record.

39
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:07,400
The main run's 95 journal entries were posted to T:0's sandbox, and T:0 matches them line by line.

40
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:12,600
Every line of this film has its record.

41
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:17,800
The proof page lists what Purser guarantees, who enforces each, and the evidence.

42
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:27,600
What is not done: the alerts go live once Twilio keys are set, and sandbox settlement is simulated.

43
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:33,200
In the Visa sandbox, a credential reused on a bigger payment was not refused.

44
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,600
There, only Purser holds the limit.

45
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:39,000
Agents do the work.

46
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,400
The CFO signs only the exceptions.

47
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:45,400
Our code checks every limit, and the rail checks again.

48
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,000
Purser, for Kit 11.

49
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,200
Try it yourself.
